          "type": "qa",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Do I need a pad, or will gravel do?",
            "answer": "<p>Gravel works for a small, light shed on flat ground. Anything heavy, anything you'll store a mower or tools in, and anything you want square in ten years is better on concrete.</p>"
          }
        },
        "q3": {
          "type": "qa",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Can you pour in a tight side yard?",
            "answer": "<p>Yes — most shed pads are in tight side yards. We wheelbarrow, pump or chute depending on access, and we'll tell you at the estimate how we'd reach it.</p>"
          }
        },
        "q4": {
          "type": "qa",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Does a shed pad need drainage?",
            "answer": "<p>It needs slope. We pour a slight fall away from the building so water doesn't sit against the base and find its way into the floor.</p>"
